 of points:**\n   - Point \\(A\\) is at \\((0, 5)\\).\n   - Point \\(C\\) is at \\((12, 0)\\).\n   - Point \\(D\\) is at \\((10.1, 0.8)\\).\n\n2. **Find the coordinates of point \\(B\\):**\n   - Since \\(B\\) is directly above \\(C\\) on the y-axis, its coordinates are \\((12, 5)\\).\n\n3. **Use the distance formula to find \\(BD\\):**\n   The distance formula between two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is:\n   \\[\n   d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n   \\]\n   Here, the coordinates of \\(B\\) are \\((12, 5)\\) and the coordinates of \\(D\\) are \\((10.1, 0.8)\\).\n\n4. **Substitute the coordinates into the distance formula:**\n   \\[\n   BD = \\sqrt{(10.1 - 12)^2 + (0.8 - 5)^2}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Simplify the expression inside the square root:**\n   \\[\n   BD = \\sqrt{(-1.9)^2 + (-4.2)^2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   BD = \\sqrt{3.61 + 17.64}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   BD = \\sqrt{21.25}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Simplify the square root:**\n   \\[\n   BD = \\sqrt{\\frac{85}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{85}}{2}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the length of segment \\(BD\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{85}}{2}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{85}}{2}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:453"}
